sed as part of the diaries  were many boxes of personal  documents from her life  which was another one birth certificates  that's another story read the chapter in  the book on birth certificates because  she not she would have one birth  certificate for her son william  which was probably the original one then  she went and had a second one done with  different names  and she did the same thing when her  second son  was born and she was constantly  playing if you will these kinds of games  but the documentation is really there's  quite a bit now as far as american  atheists are concerned um i was not very  successful  they were very protective of her i think  i would have had better luck if she  hadn't disappeared when i was writing  the book  and then they were under such siege  thinking that she'd absconded with the  money that they sort of drew up the the  drawbridge and decided they weren't  going to let anyone  near that documentation however having  said that i it worked out okay because  really there isn't much  personal material an american atheist  there's a lot of literature it's a  wonderful collection on atheism  madeline collected it but there wasn't a  lot of personal papers one thing about  madeleine madeleine wrote everything  down and got it published she had  newsletters she had magazines she had a  radio show then published transcripts in  the radio shows so there wasn't much  that madeleine thought or said that  didn't make it into print so  yes if i can follow on that question uh  was madeleine  spiritual at all did she believe in  spirituality and in examining her  diaries  do you  perceive it all over time any kind of  spiritual or even emotional growth going  on  oh  interesting ending to that question  i didn't detect very much of anything in  terms of a spiritual  understanding there's just nothing there  to deal with she was a committed as she  believed rationalist who just didn't  believe in any kind of spiritual  focus or force in the 